# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# ZClean — files git must never carry
#
# WHY THIS MATTERS MOST
#   The .env files hold the Supabase database password, the JWT signing secret
#   and the Gmail app password. Push them once and they are public — and a
#   repository's HISTORY keeps them even after a later commit deletes the file.
#   Anyone with the JWT secret can mint an admin token without a password.
#
#   Capstone submission often means putting the code on GitHub, so this file
#   has to exist BEFORE the first push.
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ── Secrets ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*/.env
*/.env.*
!*/.env.example

# ── Dependencies (reinstalled with `npm install`) ───────────────────────────
node_modules/
*/node_modules/

# ── Build output ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
dist/
build/
client/dist/

# ── Uploads: real client data, not source code ──────────────────────────────
# Payment receipts, chat photos and service images belong on the server, not
# in version control. The folders themselves are recreated on startup.
server/uploads/
uploads/

# ── Logs and local noise ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
npm-debug.log*
logs/

# ── Editors and operating systems ───────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ── Temporary ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.tmp
*.bak
.cache/
